2026-10-15 19:12 UTC — reconciled the Java `MessageExt` constructor surface.

Pinned source commit `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9` declares exactly
these public constructors: `MessageExt()` and
`MessageExt(int, long, SocketAddress, long, SocketAddress, String)`. The invoked
`messageExtPublicApi` fixture now reflects and pins both signatures. Rust
`MessageExt::new()` and `Default` map to the no-argument constructor; the
Rust-only public `new(Message)` conversion was removed. Common decoder internals
use a crate-private `from_message`; Consumer/Core product paths use no-argument
construction and inherited setters. Consumer/Core test fixtures use cfg(test)
helpers, which add no downstream API. A compile-fail doctest guards both the
removed conversion and the private helper boundary. The Phase 8 matrix and
release checklist record this bounded closure; broad P18-V01 remains open.

